# Space traversal architecture (pointer)

Full law: [`docs/docs/architecture/space-traversal.md`](../../docs/docs/architecture/space-traversal.md).

**Permanent decision:** scene document + Scene Settings **`Runtime`**
(`open-space` / `station` / `hab` / `hangar` / `flow`). Station = giant prefab
in the system host. Ship boarding: **`enter-station`** (fly-through on station
body → hangar instance) and **`exit-hangar`** (hangar → Open Space at nested
`hangar-open-space-exit` mouth). Open-air and closed stations share those
components. Far bodies cull; pilot **nav** blips stay (Combat contact blips are a separate
HUD set). Quantum bridges long burns **inside** one Star Map. **Between**
systems: Star Map **Warp Gate** (`warp-gate` → other `systemId`) — fly/quantum
to gate, then host swap; see
[Star Map](../../docs/docs/architecture/star-map.md).

When changing open-space layout, station authoring, boarding markers, quantum,
Warp Gates, culling, or nav blips, read the full doc first. Also listed in
`AGENTS.md`.
